      "textEn": "The actions of a couple are performed for the pleasure of happiness and liberation. Then there is no cessation of suffering, neither of sorrow nor of happiness. 60. Meaning of the word\n\nFor happiness—for happiness; sorrow-mokshaya—to get rid of sorrow; kurvate—they do; dampati—wife and husband;\nKriya—action; tatah—from that; anivrittiha—not getting rest; apraptiha—not getting profit; dukkhasya—of sorrow; cha—also;\nSukhasya—of happiness; cha—also. Men and women, as couples, in many ways, by mutual cooperation, to attain happiness\nand to reduce sorrow, they make plans in many ways; but\nbecause they are fulfilled by desires, their actions neither ever bring happiness nor reduce sorrow\nin any way. On the contrary, they are held responsible for the heavy sufferings. And knowing the opposite, the proud and arrogant. The self's journey, subtle, unique, and unparalleled. 61. He is released by his own splendor, by the power of sight and hearing.\nThe one who is satisfied with the knowledge of science, that person becomes my devotee. 62). Meaning of the word\n\nEvam—in this way; Viparyayam—contradictory; Buddhva—understanding; Nrinaam—of humans; Vijna-abhimaninam—those who consider themselves\ncomplete with knowledge; Atmanah—of oneself; Cha—also; Gatim—progress; Sukshmam—extremely difficult to understand;\nSthan-trayam—the three states of life (deep sleep, Dream and awakening); Vividhaam—separated from; Drishta—seen directly;\nShrutaabhih—or understood from the information of authorities; Matrabhih—from objects; Nirmuktah—having become free; Svan—from oneself; Tejasah—with discretion; Gyan-Vigyan—knowledge and this knowledge; Santhushta—fully satisfied; Mat-Bhakta—My devotee; Purusha—Man; Bhavet—Should become. Man should know that the person who is proud of their physical experience,\nthey get opposite results to the fruits imagined in waking, sleeping and deep sleep.\nMan should also understand that although it is difficult for a materialistic person to see the soul,\neven then, he is beyond all these situations and he should renounce the desire for the fruits of action in this birth and the next birth\nbased on his discretion. In this way, only by becoming experienced in divine knowledge should one become my devotee."
