      "textEn": "Etawavena manujeya yoganepunyabuddhibhih. Selfishness is known to the self, that is the vision of the other self. 63. Meaning of the word\n\nEtawan—so much; Ev—indeed; Manujaih—by humans; Yoga—through devotion to yoga, the method of connecting with God\nBy; Nipunya—skill; Buddhibih—by the wise; Swa-Artha—the ultimate purpose of life; Sarva-Atmana—in every way; Gyeyah—worthy of knowing; Yat—that; Para—of the divine God; Atma—of the self; Eka—of oneness; Darshanam—understanding. Those men who want to achieve the ultimate purpose of life should observe the supreme being\nand the soul well, which, being part and whole, are qualitatively\none. That is the greatest wisdom of life. Nothing can be truer than this. You, with faith, O king, did not disobey my words.\nKnowledge, science, and wealth, if you hold them, you will not achieve success. 64. Meaning of the word:\n\nTvam—you; Etat—this; Shraddhaya—with great faith; Rajan—Oh King; Apramattha—without being intoxicated, without reaching any other conclusion; Vachah—teaching; Mama—mine; Gnan-Vijnan-Sampannah—being well-versed in knowledge and science; Dharayan—accepting; Ashu—quickly; Siddhis—you will be able to achieve. Hey Rajan! If you, detached from material pleasures, remain attached to me with utmost faith,\nand by becoming proficient in knowledge and its practicality in life, accept this conclusion of mine,\nthen you will attain supreme perfection. Srisuka said:\n\nSrisuka said:\nTo assure, the Lord, thus, to Chitraketu, the world teacher.\nHe sees his own self as the universe, and then Hari (God) fills it. 65. Meaning of the word\n\nShri-Shuka said—Shri Shukadeva Goswami said; Assurshya—giving assurance; Bhagavan—Bhagavan; Ittham—in this way;\nChitraketum—to King Chitraketu; Jagat-guruha—the supreme guru; Pashyatah—by seeing; Tasya—his; Vishwa-Atma—the entire\nUniverse; Tat—from there; Cha—also; Antardhade—disappeared; Harih—Lord Hari. Shri Shukdev Goswami further said—In this way, after giving adv